cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyGeoVision in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software

title: "PyGeoVision: The World-Class Standalone Geospatial AI Platform"
version: 2.1.4
date-released: "2026-06-27"
url: "https://github.com/pygeovision/pygeovision"
license: Apache-2.0

abstract: >
  PyGeoVision v2.0 is a fully standalone geospatial AI platform with its own
  119-model registry, DINOv3 (12 variants, SAT-493M pre-training), Prithvi-EO-2.0
  (600M parameters), CLIP + RemoteCLIP + Moondream VLM stack, production GeoTrainer,
  DataValidator (mandatory preprocessing gate), 22 spectral indices, 51 end-to-end
  pipelines, FastAPI serving, ONNX/Jetson/AWS/Azure/GCP deployment, and 25 production
  notebooks. Integrates with PyGeoFetch (22+ satellite providers) for data acquisition
  and GeoAI (optional plugin) for extended AI capabilities.

keywords:
  - geospatial AI
  - remote sensing
  - satellite imagery
  - deep learning
  - earth observation
  - foundation models
  - DINOv3
  - Prithvi
  - change detection
  - semantic segmentation
  - SAR processing
  - spectral indices

authors:
